<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Babylon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Babylon was an ancient city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> and one of the most famous cities of the ancient world. It was the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi</a>'s Babylonian Empire and later of the Chaldean or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-empire">Neo-Babylonian Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar II</a>. It was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a> in 539 BCE and remained an important centre under the Achaemenid and Seleucid empires.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/babylon.jpg" alt="Babylon" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Stanley · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ishtar_Gate.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
